        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{25}\\int_{5 e}^{5 e^{2}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}{2\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\ln\\left(\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)\\right).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\u27f9\\,1\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $5 e$ | $5 e^{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{25}\\int_{5 e}^{5 e^{2}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}{2\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{25}\\int_{5 e}^{5 e^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int_{1}^{2}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}}\\right)|_{1}^{2} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {{u}^{2}}\\right)|_{1}^{2} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{4}({2}^{2}-{1}^{2})\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{4}(3)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
